.TH LARADOCK 1 "May 2026" "1.0" "LaraDock CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
laradock \- CLI utility to manage LaraDock Docker development environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B laradock
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B laradock
is a command-line interface to manage the Docker-based multi-PHP development environment (similar to Windows Laragon) for Linux.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all active registered projects and their PHP versions as configured in sites.txt.
.TP
.B add \fIdomain\fR [\fIphp-version\fR]
Register a new local project site. Defaults to php-82 if PHP version is not specified.
.TP
.B remove \fIdomain\fR
Deregister a project site, remove virtual host configs, certificates, and update hosts.
.TP
.B up
Start all LaraDock containers in the background.
.TP
.B down
Stop and remove all containers.
.TP
.B restart [\fIservice\fR]
Restart all services, or a specific service (like nginx, postgres, etc.).
.TP
.B ssh \fIservice\fR
Open an interactive shell inside a running container (e.g. php-82, node).
.TP
.B trust
Trust the generated local Certificate Authority (CA) root certificate on the host system.
.TP
.B install
Install the laradock CLI globally and link its man page.
.TP
.B uninstall
Uninstall the global CLI, remove system mappings, and delete CA trust certificates.
.SH FILES
.I /home/kirito/laragon/sites.txt
The registry containing active local websites.
.SH AUTHOR
Created by kirito roy.
